---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About the archive"
  description="Learn how Chronicles of the Multiverse organizes Magic: The Gathering lore, publications, and historical card references."
>
  <section class="page-banner">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Our approach</p>
      <h1>History before <em>everything.</em></h1>
      <p>An independent, non-commercial reading project about the events, people, and worlds of Magic: The Gathering.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section-spacing">
    <div class="page-shell article-column">
      <p class="eyebrow">The purpose</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">A story-first <em>archive.</em></h2>
      <p class="lead-copy">Magic has been published in sets for decades. Its fictional history, however, is richer—and less linear—than any release calendar.</p>
      <p>Our goal is to organize those stories into clear chapters. Rather than list every card in an expansion, each chapter will explain a significant historical event and show a curated group of cards that illustrate or reference it.</p>
      <h3>Two complementary timelines</h3>
      <p><strong>Story chronology</strong> traces events in the fiction. <strong>Publication chronology</strong> records when a story or reference appeared in a Magic set. For instance, Antiquities (1994) and The Brothers' War (2022) both reference the same ancient conflict.</p>
      <h3>Editorial care</h3>
      <p>We will favor original summaries, link to official sources where possible, and mark disputed or uncertain lore clearly. Illustrated chapters and card selection will be added incrementally.</p>

<h3>About the Author</h3>

<p>
  Chronicles of the Multiverse was created by
  <strong>DevIsola</strong>, an independent developer
  building a historical archive dedicated to
  the stories and lore of Magic: The Gathering.
</p>

<p>
  The project brings together storytelling,
  historical research, and web development
  to make the history of the Multiverse easier
  to discover and explore.
</p>

<p>
  The website is an independent, non-commercial
  fan initiative and is developed openly
  on GitHub.
</p>

<p>
  You can follow the project's development
  and contributions through&nbsp
  <a
    class="inline-link"
    href="https://github.com/DevIsola"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
  >
    DevIsola's GitHub profile ↗
  </a>.
</p>

      
<section
  class="support-panel"
  aria-labelledby="support-heading"
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Support the project</p>

  <h3 id="support-heading">
    Help preserve the stories of the Multiverse.
  </h3>

  <p>
    Chronicles of the Multiverse is a passion project
    built and maintained by DevIsola. Every chapter
    involves historical research, writing, card
    curation, and ongoing development.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you enjoy the archive and would like to
    support my work, you can leave an optional
    contribution through Ko-fi.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>
      The archive will remain free and accessible
      to everyone, regardless of donations.
    </strong>
  </p>

  <a
    class="support-panel__link"
    href="https://ko-fi.com/B1H328PBAR"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
  >
    <span aria-hidden="true">♥</span>
    Support on Ko-fi
    <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
  </a>
</section>

      <h3>Fan-content notice</h3>
      <p>This site is independent fan content and is not affiliated with, endorsed, or approved by Wizards of the Coast. Magic: The Gathering and associated characters, worlds, and card artwork are the property of their respective rights holders.</p>
      <p>Read the <a class="inline-link" href="https://company.wizards.com/en/legal/fancontentpolicy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wizards of the Coast Fan Content Policy ↗</a>.</p>
      <a class="button button--dark" href={withBase('timeline/')}>Explore the historical timeline <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
